{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Changes one kb.plan entry's lifecycle: finds the entry by exact claim, strips any existing lifecycle token from its tags (proposed/accepted/in-progress/blocked/completed/done/abandoned), appends the new one, and writes the whole facet through the journaled dev.code.patch_control_facet. base is the hash from board; a mismatch returns err stale_base with current_hash - reload the board and retry. Other tags and all entry fields are preserved. BLOCKED: an item the agent cannot advance without a human sits in `blocked` (step_item moves it there on STATUS: BLOCKED); it is not steppable and the plan worker skips it - moving it back to `accepted` is the human unblock. RE-APPROVAL HOOK (convergence guard): moving an item TO `accepted` is the human re-authorization - if its step_log has reached MAX_PLAN_STEPS (i.e. step_item refused it with needs_reapproval), the log is reset (prior count recorded in steps_reset) so the agent may step it again; a normal accept leaves a non-exhausted log untouched.","import":"","params":[{"name":"claim","type":"String"},{"name":"lifecycle","type":"String"},{"name":"base","type":"String"},{"name":"nn_sessionid","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"ijyjoz1a03a510268ta","readers":[],"time":1792758442283,"username":"system","writers":[]}